Step over an empty match in strsplit(perl = TRUE) by one byte unless the
input is UTF-8, so the character target stops overflowing the token
buffer on bytes-encoded input.

do_strsplit() (src/main/grep.c) advances past an empty PCRE match by
utf8clen() of the next byte (r84516, PR#18546), even for useBytes = TRUE
or native input in a single-byte locale, where the string was never
validated as UTF-8.  A byte such as 0xff makes utf8clen() claim 6 bytes:
the counting loop runs past the terminator, and the fill loop's
strncpy() writes those bytes into a token buffer of strlen(buf) + 1:

    ==5395==ERROR: AddressSanitizer: heap-buffer-overflow
    WRITE of size 4 at 0x792d892f22d2 thread T0
        #0 ___interceptor_strncpy
        #1 do_strsplit src/main/grep.c:908
        #2 bcEval_loop src/main/eval.c:8150
    0x792d892f22d2 is located 0 bytes after 2-byte region

Advance by one byte unless use_UTF8 (whose input has passed utf8Valid()),
as gsub()'s PCRE path already does.

The upstream PR also adds a regression test (tests/reg-tests-1e.R),
not carried here.

Found by OSS-Fuzz: testcase 5881106650693632 (afl_r_character,
strsplit("\xff", "|", perl = TRUE, useBytes = TRUE)).

Upstream status: r-devel/r-svn PR #376, filed 2026-10-12 (no Bugzilla
report yet).
Delete this patch once the fix lands in R trunk (ossfuzz.sh will report
it as already-applied in the meantime, which is harmless).

--- a/src/main/grep.c
+++ b/src/main/grep.c
@@ -869,11 +869,14 @@
 					  (int) strlen(bufp),
 					  0, 0, ovector, ovecsize)) >= 0) {
 #endif
-			/* Empty matches get the next char, so move by one. */
+			/* Empty matches get the next char, so move by one.
+			   Only use_UTF8 input has been validated as UTF-8;
+			   utf8clen() on an arbitrary byte claims up to 6 and
+			   would run past the terminator. */
 			if (ovector[1] > 0)
 			    bufp += ovector[1];
 			else if (*bufp)
-			    bufp += utf8clen(*bufp);
+			    bufp += use_UTF8 ? utf8clen(*bufp) : 1;
 			ntok++;
 			if (*bufp == '\0')
 			    break;
@@ -903,8 +906,8 @@
 			pt[ovector[0]] = '\0';
 			bufp += ovector[1];
 		    } else {
-			/* Match was empty. */
-			int clen = utf8clen(*bufp);
+			/* Match was empty: copy one character (see above). */
+			int clen = use_UTF8 ? utf8clen(*bufp) : 1;
 			strncpy(pt, bufp, clen);
 			pt[clen] = '\0';
 			bufp += clen;
